WEBVTT

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.160
Hibiki!

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.580
Daichi.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.770
You waiting long? Sorry 'bout that.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:29.710
It's okay.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.710
So, how'd you do? On your exam.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.020
I don't know.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.310
But you'll do well if you try harder.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.100
YOU'RE the one who can study.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.360
I'm done for, in more ways than one.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.580
That's true.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.980
But it's just a practice exam,
so there's no need to worry, right?

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:49.730
You're pretty flippant,
you son of a bitch!

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.090
Take that! And that!

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:57.630
A new "dead face" clip
has been uploaded!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.470
Okay then! Have a nice time!

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:46.010
Melancholy Sunday

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.770
Hibiki, you're goin' to college, right?

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.190
That's why you spend Sundays
taking practice tests.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.210
For now, I guess.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.500
I can't think of anything else to do.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.040
Sounds like you.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.360
Is it enough?

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.500
Daichi, if you get into college,
what will you do then?

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:16.180
Well, find somethin' I wanna do!

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.630
What do you want to do?

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:21.340
Goin' on dates, on trips...

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:25.570
And drives! I just got my license.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:26.780
You want to play around.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.440
Work is for losers!

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.920
Really? You'll have no regrets?

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.440
Well, it's like... I'm just so nervous!

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.800
I can't really do anything.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.250
Yeah, true.

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.530
Right? We're friggin' hopeless.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.120
We're just high-school students.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:49.230
Is that... really true?

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.180
Oh, that's right.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:55.220
There's something I wanted to show you.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.540
Well, wanna see?

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:57.600
What is it?

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.310
Lend me your phone. Hold on.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:03.310
Ta-daa!

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:04.860
"Nicaea"?

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.600
Yes, Nicaea!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.430
It's a secret but popular
"dead face" site!

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.860
Dead face?

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:11.730
That's right.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.920
If you register, you can see

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.440
the face of your friend when he dies!

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.430
So, when you die,

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:21.440
I'll get a picture to my
phone of your dead face?

00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:25.210
Why's it gotta be me?
But yeah, that's right.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:31.590
You know that student two years older
who died in an accident last week?

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:34.100
They say his death face appeared
right before the accident.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.320
No way, for real?

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.340
For real!

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.920
See? It's popular.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:42.070
I'll be announcing when a new
clip has been uploaded,

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.710
so be sure to come watch, 'kay?

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:47.340
Okay then! Have a nice time!

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.500
It's awesome, right? Super scary, huh?

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.240
In a way.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.620
I'm lookin' forward to the next clip.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:07.890
And then, the kicker is
so funny that... Huh?

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:08.710
What?

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:09.120
There!

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:11.720
That's Io Nitta from Class C!

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.330
Who's that? A friend?

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:18.260
No. But I sure wanna be her friend...

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.760
Looks like she's coming home
from a practice exam.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:24.470
She's cute, huh?

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:25.510
I don't know...

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:28.190
For a guy, you're just weird!

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.770
Well, she's YOUR type.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:31.980
Y-Yeah, kinda.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:41.190
Whoa! It looks like a video's
already up on Nicaea!

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.160
Let's see.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:02.600
For real?

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:10.510
This...

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:15.340
It's a joke, right?

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.860
The site's just for fun.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.400
How do they Photoshop this stuff?

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.210
The clip was filmed right here.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.750
Stop it!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.280
Apologies for the wait.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.110
The train bound of Oshiage will
soon arrive at Track 2.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.120
Please stand back and wait
behind the yellow line.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.210
Daichi, wanna leave the station?

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.550
Huh? Uh, yeah.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.990
Thank you for using Nicaea!

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.420
At this rate, you'll die.

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:05.270
But if you like, I can
give you another chance.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.230
You still want to live?

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:15.760
Okay, okay! I've confirmed
your STRONG will to live.

00:07:17.130 --> 00:07:20.090
The Demon Summoning app
has been downloaded.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.510
Good luck, 'kay?

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:42.550
Th-This... Everything was
normal just a minute ago.

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:44.710
Daichi!

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.040
The heck is this?

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:53.640
Daichi, you're bleeding!

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:54.590
You okay?

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:55.920
Uh, yeah.

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.430
We have to call for help.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:03.700
Oh, yeah.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:07.180
Daichi, over there!

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.250
A survivor!

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:10.080
Are you all right?

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.350
What is that?!

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.100
Nitta!

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:49.670
Stay back!

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:08.770
What the...?!

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.200
A demon?

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.660
Here, this way!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.770
Hibiki! Hurry!

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.010
It's protecting us.

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:45.870
Hibiki!

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.400
What is that?

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:55.620
Let's go.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:56.690
Yeah.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:09.420
Did you see that just now?
What was that thing?

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.300
Because of this?

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:17.150
It's that monster!

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:21.490
What is this app?

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:23.290
Demons...

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:24.780
It's Nicaea.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:31.270
Earlier, the instant the train derailed,
I was asked if I wanted to die.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:32.780
Me, too.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.530
Actually, me too.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:37.960
I said I didn't want to die,

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:42.240
so I think Nicaea forcibly
downloaded this app.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:45.200
Huh? Nicaea did? What for?

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:46.660
I don't know.

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.020
No way!

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:57.710
No...

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:08.030
The demon displayed
here didn't attack us.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:10.620
Is that a function of the app?

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.020
So, what about the one that DID attack?

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:17.690
Maybe we're not the only ones
made to download that app.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:22.640
But those people died,
and then the demons just came out.

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:24.450
What are you talking about?

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:26.370
I don't know.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.230
But we were definitely attacked.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:32.080
A friend of mine invited me.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:36.050
That's how... I knew about the site.

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.840
But I didn't register.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.980
Neither did we.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.490
We can't stay here. Can you walk?

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:47.240
Yes.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:48.530
Let's get out of the station.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.650
Move that. Hurry!

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:55.150
Sir!

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.660
This is an emergency broadcast.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:02.380
Today, a wide-scale disaster
occurred around 1:00 pm.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.380
It can't be.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.160
The city's all busted up!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.120
Details are still scarce,
but the city center

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.130
It's terrible!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:09.370
appears to have suffered
tremendous damage.

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:11.960
Was this because of the demons?

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:14.030
Repeating: Today, a wide-scale disaster
occurred around 1:00 pm.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.750
Demon Summoning

00:12:14.030 --> 00:12:17.960
Just... What is going on?

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:33.730
Repeating: Today, a wide-scale disaster
occurred around 1:00 pm.

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:39.610
Details are still scarce, but the city center
appears to have suffered tremendous damage.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.830
The station area is currently unusable!

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:43.880
There's no telling when
operations will resume!

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.210
Hello, Mom?

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:48.140
Yeah, I'm at Shibuya.

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:49.500
I'm with Hibiki.

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:54.090
Hello? Hello?!

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:56.580
What do we do? It won't work.

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:58.710
Move! Please stand aside!

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.770
A subway train overturned.

00:13:06.770 --> 00:13:07.410
There are still survivors--

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:08.620
Hey, get back.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:09.640
Please stand aside.

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.470
Who the heck are you?

00:13:11.740 --> 00:13:14.660
In accordance with Article 404 of the
Special Disaster Management Act,

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.580
we are assuming command of this site.

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.980
Article 404? What are you talking about?

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:21.670
-Hey, you! Stand back!
-That's no reason to stop our rescue efforts.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:22.820
Get out of the way!

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.920
The situation remains dangerous.

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.580
Please respect our authority.

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:27.570
This is ridiculous!

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.070
Please stop this.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.990
This is no time for arguing!

00:13:29.710 --> 00:13:30.990
Hey, Hibiki!

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:34.430
It looks like your and
my families evacuated.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:38.060
But I lost signal as we were talking,
so that's all I know.

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:39.300
Is that so?

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:44.210
Nitta.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:48.630
So, no signal?

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:49.720
Yeah.

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:54.390
Where is your house?

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:57.620
It's in Ariake.

00:13:57.620 --> 00:13:58.760
That's far.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:01.260
And we probably can't use the trains.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:08.630
Let's get away from here.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:10.880
But where should we go?

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.090
To your house.

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:12.710
Huh?

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:16.090
Y-Yeah. Staying here
won't solve anything.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.050
Let's try getting as far as we can.

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:25.630
I'm grateful for your cooperation.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:30.390
The Setagaya area is no good.

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.440
There's extensive damage
and several casualties.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:34.480
I see.

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.660
It's started, hasn't it?

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:39.840
This has been anticipated
since antiquity.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:41.100
Don't go getting scared now.

00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:45.260
We've received multiple reports
of Case D manifestation.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.590
As of now, use of the
Summoning programming at

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:51.710
your own discretion is permitted.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:52.200
Ma'am!

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.430
Sako to base.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:01.050
We are shifting to Readiness State 2.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.290
Please refresh the system.

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:05.600
Case D isn't the problem.

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:08.470
Humankind must survive Judgment Day,

00:15:08.710 --> 00:15:12.320
even if it means using those demons.

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:29.540
Dammit. Why can't I delete this app?

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:32.990
Um... Shijima and Kuze, was it?

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:34.840
I'm sorry.

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.240
I'm sure you're worried
about your families.

00:15:37.510 --> 00:15:40.220
You shouldn't worry about me.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:42.010
No, it's fine.

00:15:42.010 --> 00:15:44.060
It looks like our families
are safe for now.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:45.420
After what's happened...

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.770
We should stay together until we know

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:50.510
more about this app.

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:13.190
Still no signal?

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:14.320
Yeah.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:17.560
If I knew this would happen,

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.410
I wouldn't have taken the practice exam.

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:24.800
I told the demon I didn't want to die,

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:26.250
so maybe we've been possessed.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:28.270
I don't think so.

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:32.280
I feel we're being tested somehow.

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:34.840
By whom?

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.740
I don't know. But that's
the feeling I get.

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:40.030
Hey!

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:44.520
I got some drinks from
the store over there.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.330
Thank goodness.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:49.510
Daichi, you're no good
at rock-paper-scissors.

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:50.330
Shut up!

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:01.330
Here.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.760
That's 10-0, huh?

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:10.230
What the...?

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:12.380
What is that?

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:13.620
A UFO?

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:22.100
What's going on?

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:27.940
That...!

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.240
This is bad!

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.430
It's dangerous! Everyone, please run!

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:33.750
Ah! Chappy!

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:38.020
Run for it!

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:43.780
Nitta!

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:45.760
Hang in there!

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:46.590
My leg.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.280
It targets you if you move.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:11.660
Where's Daichi?

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:19.460
What is this?

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:20.310
A demon?

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.280
Nitta! The Summoning app!

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:25.580
The demon that came out
from that didn't attack us.

00:18:25.880 --> 00:18:28.260
It could be dangerous,
but right now it's all we've got!

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:29.540
Okay!

00:18:44.030 --> 00:18:46.600
It really is protecting us.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.260
That's going to explode again!

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.740
A new "dead face" clip
has been uploaded.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:02.990
Th-This is...

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:04.490
Daichi!

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:14.960
Oh, no!

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:20.260
I'll save you both!

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:21.730
Shijima!

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:22.590
Daichi!

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:25.810
You damn monster!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:26.890
Stop!

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:44.960
Daichi!

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:55.590
What's that?

00:19:55.770 --> 00:19:58.670
Unregistered D data confirmed in
the area of Shimbashi Station.

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:01.020
It's a different format
from our program.

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:02.440
The structural data is
completely different.

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:03.610
It can't be measured!

00:20:03.610 --> 00:20:04.820
Switch over to Osaka!

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:06.350
Receiving observational data!

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:11.070
Manifesting! It's an Avatar: Byakko!

00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:17.940
Byakko?!

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:21.030
Who could have manifested
something that powerful?

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:26.170
Get that thing!

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:42.840
Crap! Move, dammit!

00:21:23.770 --> 00:21:25.270
We did it?

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:30.790
It's gone.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:32.770
Daichi!

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:37.020
Daichi...

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:39.200
Hey!

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:43.030
Daichi!

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:49.920
There... was another one.

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:57.980
That boy.

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:01.750
HE summoned Byakko?

00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:03.760
Secure them.

00:22:07.730 --> 00:22:11.990
We are special government organization,
the Japan Meteorological Society.

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:12.980
AKA, "JP's."

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:15.770
We're taking you into custody.

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:18.390
JP's?

00:22:20.910 --> 00:22:22.030
There you are...

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:25.420
O Sparkling One.

00:24:00.090 --> 00:24:02.690
The one you defeated today was...

00:24:02.690 --> 00:24:04.430
What... happened to Daichi?

00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:06.730
